  "id": "visitation-rights",
  "term": "visitation rights",
  "definition": "Visitation rights are the legal arrangements about a child’s contact or visits, usually considered alongside custody and residence in family law proceedings. In psychology-related forensic evaluations, questions about visitation rights are examined with the child’s best interests and possible effects on the child’s well-being in mind.",
